  "user": "Fine. Back to that charge — what do I do next?",
  "answer": "Here is what I found on account ACC-1005. There are two settled card charges from TechMart Online, both EUR 240.00:\n\n- **TX-0401**, 20 July 2026, EUR 240.00\n- **TX-0402**, 14 July 2026, EUR 240.00\n\nBefore I check eligibility or open anything, I need you to confirm which charge this is about, because I can't tell from the records here which one we were looking at.\n\nAlso, the reason code matters:\n- If the goods were never delivered, the matching code is **goods_not_received**.\n- If a service was never provided, the code is **service_not_rendered**.\n- If you were charged twice for the same purchase, the code is **duplicate_charge**. The two identical EUR 240 charges could fit that case.\n\nPlease tell me the transaction ID and which of these describes your situation. I'll then run the eligibility check. If it passes, I'll show you the details and wait for your explicit go-ahead before opening the dispute, since that step can't be undone.",
